\title{NECModel: Treatment Sequencing in Small Bowel Neuroendocrine Tumours}
\description{
A continuous-time microsimulation model comparing sequences of peptide receptor radionuclide therapy (PRRT), everolimus, and cabozantinib for patients with small bowel neuroendocrine tumours who progress on somatostatin analogues, and tools for a decision analysis under deep uncertainty. Transition times are drawn from non-homogeneous Poisson point processes; the model propagates probabilistic parameter uncertainty and uncertainty sets for treatment-effect attenuation and the incidence of post-PRRT myelodysplastic syndrome and acute myeloid leukaemia (MDS/AML) to mean overall survival, progression-free survival, and MDS/AML incidence. Treatment sequences are compared with choice functions for decisions under ambiguity (maximality, interval dominance, optimism, pessimism, Hurwicz) and summarised as Hasse diagrams.
}
